\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Rise, my soul, gird thee with pow'r;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Watch! To pray'r be take thee;
\par Lest the sudden evil hour
\par Unawares o'er-take thee;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Satan's prey soon are they
\par Who make no endeavour,
\par Watch not, pray not ever.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  But first, rouse thee and awake
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 From thy sinful slumber,
\par Else will follow in its wake
\par Burdens which encumber.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Take thou heed! Utmost need,
\par Death in sin might find thee
\par Ere thou look behind thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Wake, arouse! Else can the Lord
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Not enlighten, teach thee;
\par Nor thou see His holy word
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Shine in splendour round thee.\tab 
\par God demands eyes and hands
\par Open for the offers
\par He so richly proffers.\tab 
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With thy watching, mingle prayer;
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Watching, praying, waiting.
\par God rids thee from slothful care
\par In love unabating.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And at length His great strength
\par Helps in our endeavour
\par \pard        To be His forever.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

